      {
        "id": 6302571949,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "action_name": "commented on",
        "target_id": 4189392795,
        "target_iid": 4189392795,
        "target_type": "DiffNote",
        "author_id": 21826781,
        "target_title": "feat(govern): redact values assigned to credential-like names in text",
        "created_at": "2026-11-09T03:58:40.265Z",
        "note": {
          "id": 4189392795,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The name pattern allows an unescaped quote after the name, but not an escaped one. In `curl -d \"{\\\"password\\\": \\\"hunter2hunter2\\\"}\"` the name `password` is followed by `\\`, so `[:=]` fails and the value is never read. `assignedValue` handles `\\\"...\\\"` values, but a key quoted that way never reaches it. JSON written inside a shell command is a common shape for agent commands. Allowing backslashes before the quote fixes it.\n```suggestion:-0+0\n\t\tre:    regexp.MustCompile(`\\b([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_\\-]*)(?:\\\\*[\"'])?[ \\t]*[:=][ \\t]*`),\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 21826781,
            "username": "GitLabDuo",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "GitLab Duo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/GitLabDuo"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-11-09T03:58:40.175Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-11-09T03:58:40.175Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 564213685,
